lines+=['','## Hand review and correction','', '[REVIEW.md](REVIEW.md) lists every company, orgnr, website/profile URL, proof type, verbatim saved excerpt, verdict and reason. JSON ledgers retain hashes and source URLs. Review inspected the original live source bodies and registry context; social platforms were not fetched.','', 'Raw website verdicts: 10 correct, 4 wrong, 9 doubtful. Raw social profile verdicts: 41 correct, 4 wrong, 13 doubtful. Correct means the reviewed source supports company attribution; it is not a universal precision guarantee. Conservative runtime rules may withhold genuine but unproven aliases.','', 'Generic corrections, with no company-specific exceptions:', '', '- Removed name-only legal-masthead and unique-name-domain publication. This prevents punctuation-collapsed namesakes, placeholders and bare app-shell titles from proving ownership.', '- Email-only proof now requires the registered non-free-mail domain to occur for exactly one registry entity, not fewer than five. Ice Drift staff email on a domain shared by four entities did not identify Straumsnes Utvikling as site owner.', '- Additional contact proofs reject blank bodies and short Her kommer placeholders.', '- Restored company/verified-brand handle matching for social profiles. Header/footer/sameAs presence alone cannot authorize founder, artist, sister/group or agency profiles. Facebook plugin support remains, with the same attribution check.', '', 'Regression coverage includes placeholders, URL/email repetition, blank shells, shared employee email, unrelated footer handles, plus existing named wrong-company/group/foreign-orgnr tests. The complete suite passes: **1,259 passed in 374.14 s**. The cleanup-only merged revision earlier passed 1,251 tests; only search-specific tests/function were removed then.','', '## Offline re-derivation after corrections','', 'No third live benchmark was run. `scripts/r3_rederive.py` rechecks hash-verified saved candidate HTML with current proof and social functions. It never makes requests; original outputs are untouched. Retired proofs are withheld unless an existing retained proof can be established from saved pages; website-derived claims and site jobs/articles are conservatively withheld when the site loses proof. Exact-name registry/Wikidata social claims keep the existing direct-match path.','', '| Offline conservative projection | Count |','|---|---:|']
lines += [f'| {k} | {projection[k]} |' for k in ('websites','social_companies','jobs','activity','facts')]
lines += ['',f'Retained reviewed gains: **{len(kept_web)} website companies**, **{final["new_social_companies_retained"]} new social companies**, **{len(kept_social)} new social profiles**. All retained reviewed gains are correct: **0 wrong, 0 doubtful**. Raw candidate 129 websites / 63 social companies becomes an offline conservative 107 / 48; jobs and activity remain 3 / 1000. HTTP and wall time are only the pre-correction live measurements above; they are not measurements of the narrowed runtime.','', '| Retained new proof | Count |','|---|---:|']+[f'| {k} | {v} |' for k,v in sorted(proofs.items())]
lines+=['','| Retained new candidate source | Count |','|---|---:|']+[f'| {k} | {v} |' for k,v in sorted(sources.items())]
